---
import DocumentationLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentationLayout.astro';
import ImplementationSupport from './ImplementationSupport.astro';
import PreviewControls from './PreviewControls.astro';
import AuthenticationPreview from './AuthenticationPreview.astro';
import {SignUpBlock,PasswordRecoveryBlock} from '../dmf-ui/blocks';
import {CodeSnippet} from '../dmf-ui/code-block';
import {blocks} from '../../data/blocks';
import catalog from '../../../contracts/catalog.json';
interface Props {slug:'sign-up'|'password-recovery';}
const {slug}=Astro.props,block=blocks.find(b=>b.slug===slug)!,record=catalog.blocks.find(b=>b.slug===slug)!,react=catalog.react.blocks.find(b=>b.name===block.title)!,signup=slug==='sign-up';
---
<DocumentationLayout title={block.title} description={block.description} section="blocks" crumbs={[{name:'Blocks',href:'/blocks/'},{name:block.title}]} toc={[{id:'preview',title:'Preview'},{id:'usage',title:'Astro and React'},{id:'api',title:'API and defaults'},{id:'states',title:'States'},{id:'ownership',title:'Host responsibilities'}]}>
<h1 class="docs-block-title">{block.title}</h1><p class="docs-lead">{block.description}</p><ImplementationSupport slug={slug} kind="block"/>
<section id="preview" class="docs-section"><h2>Live preview</h2><PreviewControls/><AuthenticationPreview kind={slug}/></section>
<section id="usage" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Astro and React usage</h2><p>Import shared styles once and render inside .dmf-ui. action is a required host-owned POST destination, also when a React onSubmit handler intercepts it. No authentication endpoint is shipped.</p><CodeSnippet code={block.usage} language="astro" title="Astro source" wrap/><CodeSnippet code={`import {${block.title}} from '@dmf-ui/react';\nimport '@dmf-ui/react/styles.css';\n\n<${block.title} id="account-${slug}" action="/account/${slug}" />`} language="tsx" title="React web alpha" wrap/><p>Both adapters use native, uncontrolled fields. email is an initial/reset value. Password fields have no initial-value API. Custom fields use the Astro fields slot or React fields prop; footer and default content use named slots or footer/children. Give repeated forms distinct descriptive titles so their named landmarks are distinguishable. Supply unique IDs and labels for extension fields. Do not nest forms.</p></section>
<section id="api" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Public API and authored defaults</h2><p>Composes {block.components.join(', ')}. React uses its existing Button with a separate pending status, as SignInBlock does. There are no new visual variants or density modes; native form attributes, class/style and React refs/events remain available.</p><CodeSnippet code={record.declaration} language="ts" title="Astro Props" wrap/><CodeSnippet code={react.types[0].declaration} language="ts" title="React Props" wrap/><div class="docs-table-scroll"><table class="docs-options"><thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Authored default</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.entries(record.defaults).map(([key,value])=><tr><td><code>{key}</code></td><td><code>{String(value)}</code></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="states" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Errors, pending, disabled and completion</h2><p>pending disables the fieldset and marks the form busy. Capture values before disabling it. disabled makes the fields unavailable; submitDisabled guards only the submit action. Field errors connect through aria-invalid and aria-describedby; form errors use an alert. All labels, help, error headings and status copy can be localized.</p>{signup?<><p>confirmPassword is opt-in. Its required native field uses new-password autocomplete; matching and password policy are host decisions. Optional terms links do not imply consent or a universal legal requirement.</p><SignUpBlock id="signup-errors" title="Registration validation example" action="/account/sign-up" disabled confirmPassword error="Illustrative host validation feedback." fieldErrors={{email:'Review this email address.',confirmPassword:'The host must validate confirmation.'}}/><SignUpBlock id="signup-pending" title="Registration pending example" action="/account/sign-up" pending/></>:<><p>complete replaces the input group with generic instructions in a persistent status region. The library does not infer whether an account exists. A host changing complete should move focus to the completion paragraph when the initiating control disappears, especially after asynchronous work. The paragraph has a stable id ending in -completion and tabIndex -1 in this state. Initial server-rendered completion requires no autofocus.</p><PasswordRecoveryBlock id="recovery-errors" title="Recovery validation example" action="/account/recovery" disabled error="Illustrative request failure." fieldErrors={{email:'Review this address.'}}/><PasswordRecoveryBlock id="recovery-pending" title="Recovery pending example" action="/account/recovery" pending/><PasswordRecoveryBlock id="recovery-complete" title="Recovery instruction example" action="/account/recovery" complete/></>}</section>
<section id="ownership" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Responsive layout, accessibility and host responsibilities</h2><p>Fields stack within a focused 28rem maximum width and shrink with the host container. Logical spacing supports RTL. Preserve visible focus and test long localized copy, enlarged text, keyboard navigation and your extension fields. Native POST and validation work without JavaScript against a real endpoint; native reset restores authored defaults. Status announcements and field relations are scoped evidence, not spoken screen-reader acceptance.</p><p>{block.limitations}</p><p>The host owns password policy, confirmation checks, CSRF, rate limits, account creation, sessions and recovery delivery. Do not log credentials or expose account existence through recovery responses. Recovery requests are separate from resetting a password after host credential validation.</p><p>Nova/Neutral defaults and existing semantic preset tokens are unchanged. CB/HUI white filled-primary labels retain their approximately 2.57:1/4.29:1 contrast exceptions; these are not WCAG AA passes. These Blocks retain filled-primary submits and do not expose a submit-variant prop. For a different action treatment, compose a host form from the existing components and test its states. Firefox, Safari, physical devices and spoken AT remain separate unverified checks for these new Blocks.</p><p><a href="/examples/authentication/">Try the composed authentication example</a> · <a href="/docs/authentication/">Authentication workflow pattern</a> · <a href="/blocks/sign-in/">Existing SignInBlock</a> · <a href="/docs/implementation-paths/">Install and select an adapter</a></p></section>
</DocumentationLayout>
